  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for increased South-South cooperation between Brazil and African Low-Income Countries, to reduce poverty and promote inclusive development of vulnerable populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Support for increased South-South cooperation between Brazil and African Low-Income Countries, to reduce poverty and promote inclusive development of vulnerable populations is a component of Building Brazil&#x2019;s Development Impact in Low Income Countries reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xA3;2,517,414. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Public sector policy and administrative management, Social Protection, Women&apos;s rights organisations and movements, and government institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
